# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD is hs-start.sh: it boots rsyslog/cron/mysql/apache2, the
# planted backdoor listener and sshd (all with their vulnerable config), then
# execs `sleep infinity`. So:
#   * every daemon is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what makes
#     the "fixed the config but never restarted the service" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting sshd/apache/mysql cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART/RELOAD the service, not merely
# start it if absent - the service is already up with the vulnerable config.
